1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,360
Volume with a swipe.

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,560
The round button: swipe
it, tap it, move it.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,227
Meet the round button.

4
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:08,481
In the Simple style, a small round
button sits on the edge of your screen,

5
00:00:08,521 --> 00:00:09,360
on top of every app.

6
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:10,475
Swipe up on it.

7
00:00:10,515 --> 00:00:12,975
Each bit you swipe turns
the volume up a step.

8
00:00:13,015 --> 00:00:14,606
The level shows on the button,

9
00:00:14,646 --> 00:00:17,160
and Android’s volume
slider comes up beside it.

10
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,375
Swipe down to turn it down.

11
00:00:19,415 --> 00:00:23,560
Swipe the other way and it
steps back down just as quickly.

12
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,134
Tap it for the volume slider.

13
00:00:26,174 --> 00:00:30,760
A tap brings up Android’s own
volume slider, ready to drag.

14
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,029
Hold it to pick it up.

15
00:00:32,069 --> 00:00:34,408
Keep your finger on it until
it dims and shows arrows.

16
00:00:34,448 --> 00:00:37,360
The long-press menu opens too, and
steps aside as soon as you move.

17
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,485
Drag it anywhere, then let go.

18
00:00:39,525 --> 00:00:42,466
Up or down the edge, or
across to the other side.

19
00:00:42,506 --> 00:00:44,960
Let go and it settles on the nearer edge.

20
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:50,310
Up next: The Quick slider.
